The provided code snippet is a part of the `LibraryManager` class in the `Emby.Server.Implementations.Library` namespace. The `LogDebug` method is an extension method provided by the `Microsoft.Extensions.Logging` namespace.

To write unit tests for this code, we need to mock the dependencies of the `LibraryManager` class and verify that the `LogDebug` method is called with the correct parameters.

Here's an example of how you can write a unit test for the `LogDebug` method:

```csharp
using Emby.Server.Implementations.Library;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;
using Moq;
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Threading;
using Xunit;

namespace Emby.Server.Implementations.Library.Tests
{
    public class LibraryManagerTests
    {
        [Fact]
        public void LogDebug_CalledWithCorrectParameters()
        {
            // Arrange
            var loggerMock = new Mock<ILogger<LibraryManager>>();
            var libraryManager = new LibraryManager(
                Mock.Of<IServerApplicationHost>(),
                Mock.Of<ILoggerFactory>(),
                Mock.Of<ITaskManager>(),
                Mock.Of<IUserManager>(),
                Mock.Of<IServerConfigurationManager>(),
                Mock.Of<IUserDataManager>(),
                new Lazy<ILibraryMonitor>(() => Mock.Of<ILibraryMonitor>()),
                Mock.Of<IFileSystem>(),
                new Lazy<IProviderManager>(() => Mock.Of<IProviderManager>()),
                new Lazy<IUserViewManager>(() => Mock.Of<IUserViewManager>()),
                Mock.Of<IMediaEncoder>(),
                Mock.Of<IItemRepository>(),
                Mock.Of<IItemPersistenceService>(),
                Mock.Of<INextUpService>(),
                Mock.Of<IItemCountService>(),
                Mock.Of<ILinkedChildrenService>(),
                Mock.Of<IImageProcessor>(),
                new NamingOptions(),
                Mock.Of<IDirectoryService>(),
                Mock.Of<IPeopleRepository>(),
                Mock.Of<IPathManager>(),
                new DotIgnoreIgnoreRule()
            );
            libraryManager._logger = loggerMock.Object;

            var item = new BaseItem { Id = Guid.NewGuid(), Name = "Test Item" };
            var metadataPath = Path.GetTempFileName();

            // Act
            libraryManager.DeleteItem(item, new DeleteOptions());

            // Assert
            loggerMock.Verify(l => l.LogDebug(
                "Deleting metadata path, Type: {Type}, Name: {Name}, Path: {Path}, Id: {Id}",
                item.GetType().Name,
                item.Name,
                metadataPath,
                item.Id),
                Times.Once);
        }
    }
}
```

This test creates a mock `ILogger<LibraryManager>` and sets it as the `_logger` field of the `LibraryManager` instance. It then calls the `DeleteItem` method and verifies that the `LogDebug` method is called with the correct parameters.

Note that this test assumes that the `DeleteItem` method calls the `LogDebug` method with the correct parameters. If this is not the case, the test will fail.

Also, note that this test uses the `Moq` library to create mock objects for the dependencies of the `LibraryManager` class. This allows us to isolate the `LibraryManager` class and test its behavior in isolation.

